These are the official binaries of JAGS 5.x for macOS, which
install to a versioned /opt/jags directory structure. The
majority of users will want to use the combined installer:

- JAGS-5.0.0-universal.pkg

This is a signed universal (x86_64 + arm64) package installer
that has been built for binary compatibility with the “Big Sur”
and “Sonoma” releases of R for macOS (versions 4.3.0 and onwards).
It contains three different builds of JAGS with varying BLAS
linkage and multi-threading capabilities, along with a build
of JAGS 4.3.2 that is provided for backwards compatibility.
The installer includes detailed descriptions of the included
builds and utilities on the welcome page - please do read this.

The following architecture and build specific installers are
also provided:

- JAGS-5.0.0-vecLib-single-aarch64.pkg
- JAGS-5.0.0-vecLib-single-x86_64.pkg

These each contain a single build of JAGS corresponding to the
BLAS linkage (Apple's vecLib) and single threading used for
previous macOS builds of JAGS, but otherwise using the same
build environment as for the combined installer. These
installers will not remove any existing version of JAGS 4.x
that you may already have installed on your system.

The build process for the installers is self-documented by the
build scripts, which are maintained on the following GitHub
repository:  https://github.com/mdenwood/JAGS-build-macOS

If you encounter problems with installation of JAGS on macOS then
please use the following JAGS discussion forum thread for help:
https://sourceforge.net/p/mcmc-jags/discussion/610037/thread/115edca29d/ 

